\f0\b \cf0 What v12 changes, all labelled in the patch:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The jet suits each voice's pitch.
\f1\b0  After each model build, each voice now also gets its own flue-to-labium distance, from 7.5 mm at 196 Hz down to 2.6 mm at 1245 Hz. A longer jet lets the low voices sound their real pitch instead of squealing.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Air matched to each pitch.
\f1\b0  The SENDPRESSURE scaling now gives each voice its own maximum: 40, 55, 70, 90, 110, 135, 165 and 200 Pa from low to high. The 100/600 split is gone. The air floor still keeps every bird warbling continuously.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Voice routing fixed.
\f1\b0  gate outlet k now drives voice k, so the air, the activity fader and the pitch wander all act on the same bird and the same wedge.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Gentler wander.
\f1\b0  The default maximum is 300 cents (\'b1 a minor third), and 
\f2\fs26 mc.pitchshift~
\f1\fs24  now runs at 
\f2\fs26 @quality better
\f1\fs24 .\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Darker, distinct timbres.
\f1\b0  Each voice keeps its own bore flare (
\f2\fs26 radius1
\f1\fs24 ). The damping of high partials (
\f2\fs26 freq-loss
\f1\fs24 ) is raised to between 1.2 and 4, and the breath noise is lowered to 0.08 at most.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Anti-screech lowpass.
\f1\b0  An 
\f2\fs26 mc.onepole~ 3500.
\f1\fs24  sits after the pitch shift. Lower it for a mellower sound, or raise it to about 6000 Hz for more air.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The physics rule is approximate, so tune by ear in this order:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A voice is silent or only breathy:
\f1\b0  raise its pressure (the per-voice 
\f2\fs26 scale
\f1\fs24  in SENDPRESSURE) or shorten its jet distance a little.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A voice still squeals:
\f1\b0  lengthen its jet distance or lower its pressure.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Everything is still too bright:
\f1\b0  lower the lowpass.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
